    {
      "section": "hero.split",
      "variant": "padded",
      "content": {
        "title": "Security built into every layer of Lattice",
        "lead": "Lattice protects your code, credentials and metadata with encryption, strict access controls and continuous monitoring, so your team can move fast on the platform without trading away the safeguards that you need.",
        "primary": {
          "label": "Choose how to get started",
          "href": "#",
          "opensDialog": true
        },
        "secondary": {
          "label": "Talk to security",
          "href": "/contact"
        },
        "media": {
          "assetRole": "photo.composite-scene",
          "alt": "Illustration: an engineer reviewing a model at a desk",
          "ref": "/assets/pages/photos/photo-2.svg"
        }
      },
      "motion": {
        "pattern": "stroke.draw-on",
        "reducedMotionFallback": "render-final-state"
      },
      "style": {
        "strokeShape": "stroke.s4",
        "strokeGradient": "gradient.01",
        "leadSize": "default",
        "columns": "6/6",
        "bottomPadding": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "section": "content.media-split",
      "variant": "media-left",
      "content": {
        "title": "Your data stays in your warehouse at all times",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Lattice compiles and orchestrates the SQL that runs inside your own data platform, so the rows you transform never need to leave it. The platform stores code, run logs and metadata about your models rather than copies of your data, and every connection uses short-lived, scoped credentials that you control and can revoke at any moment."
        ],
        "media": {
          "assetRole": "photo.composite-scene",
          "alt": "Illustration: a developer pairing over a laptop",
          "ref": "/assets/pages/photos/photo-8.svg"
        }
      },
      "motion": {
        "pattern": "reveal.fade-up",
        "reducedMotionFallback": "show-immediately"
      },
      "style": {
        "columns": "5/7",
        "topPadding": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "section": "content.media-split",
      "variant": "text-left",
      "content": {
        "title": "Controls designed for the needs of regulated industries",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Single sign-on, role-based permissions, audit logs and private networking options are available on every enterprise plan. Administrators decide who can view, edit or deploy each project, and every change is recorded with who made it and when. Teams in finance, healthcare and the public sector use these controls to meet internal policy as well as external review, without slowing their analysts down."
        ],
        "media": {
          "assetRole": "photo.composite-scene",
          "alt": "Illustration: a consultant preparing a migration plan",
          "ref": "/assets/pages/photos/photo-10.svg"
        }
      },
      "motion": {
        "pattern": "reveal.fade-up",
        "reducedMotionFallback": "show-immediately"
      },
      "style": {
        "columns": "7/5",
        "topPadding": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "section": "company.compliance-rows",
      "variant": "default",
      "content": {
        "title": "Our audits",
        "rows": [
          {
            "badge": {
              "assetRole": "award.badge",
              "alt": "Trustframe placeholder",
              "ref": "/assets/pages/badges/badge-1.svg"
            },
            "title": "Trustframe",
            "body": "An independent audit firm reviews our security, availability and confidentiality controls every year and issues a full report covering the twelve months before the review. The report describes each control, how the auditors tested it and any exceptions they found, along with our response to them. The scope covers the hosted platform, the infrastructure it runs on, the people who operate it and the vendors we rely on, and it is mapped to the common criteria used by most enterprise procurement teams. Customers and prospects under a confidentiality agreement can [request the latest report](/contact) through their account team at any time. A bridge letter covering the months since the last audit period is also available on request, and we share the next audit date well in advance."
          },
          {
            "badge": {
              "assetRole": "award.badge",
              "alt": "Cloudward placeholder",
              "ref": "/assets/pages/badges/badge-2.svg"
            },
            "title": "Cloudward",
            "body": "Our information security management system is certified against a placeholder cloud standard that covers risk assessment, asset management, supplier review, incident handling and continual improvement. The certificate is renewed every three years with surveillance audits in between, and the scope includes every production environment that runs the hosted platform, the teams who operate it and the offices they work from. Findings from each audit are tracked to closure by our governance team and reported to leadership every quarter, together with the status of any open remediation work and the owner responsible for it, so nothing is left without a clear owner and a realistic next step. [Contact us](/contact) for the current certificate and statement of applicability."
          },
          {
            "badge": {
              "assetRole": "award.badge",
              "alt": "Openaudit placeholder",
              "ref": "/assets/pages/badges/badge-7.svg"
            },
            "title": "Openaudit",
            "body": "A placeholder controls report for teams that need a lighter summary of our security program to share with their own stakeholders and procurement reviewers. It covers the same control areas as the full audit report, including access management, change management, encryption, monitoring and vendor oversight, but it is written for a general audience and can be shared without a confidentiality agreement. Many customers attach it to internal risk reviews and vendor questionnaires, which shortens procurement for both sides. The summary is refreshed after every annual audit and lists the period it covers on the first page, so reviewers always know how current it is and which version they are reading. [Download a copy](/contact) whenever you need one."
          },
          {
            "badge": {
              "assetRole": "award.badge",
              "alt": "Payshield placeholder",
              "ref": "/assets/pages/badges/badge-9.svg"
            },
            "title": "Payshield",
            "body": "Payments for self-serve plans are processed by a placeholder provider that holds the highest level of card-industry validation. Lattice never stores full card numbers on its own systems: the payment form is served directly by the provider, and our platform only ever receives a token that identifies the card for future charges. Invoices, receipts and billing contacts are managed from the account settings page, where administrators can update payment details, download past invoices and switch to invoiced billing on annual plans. Every change to billing details is recorded in the audit log, and only administrators can view it. Receipts are emailed to the billing contact as soon as a charge clears. [Billing questions](/contact) go straight to our finance team."
          },
          {
            "badge": {
              "assetRole": "award.badge",
              "alt": "Global seal placeholder",
              "ref": "/assets/pages/badges/badge-8.svg"
            },
            "title": "Global seal",
            "body": "Our cross-border transfer practices follow a placeholder framework for moving personal data between regions, with standard contractual terms available on request. We assess each transfer for the protections available in the destination country, document the supplementary measures we apply, and review those assessments whenever the legal landscape changes. Customers can choose to keep all project metadata in a single region, and support staff outside that region only see what a specific ticket requires. Our transfer register is kept current, reviewed by counsel every quarter, and shared with enterprise customers during security reviews. [Contact legal](/contact) with any questions about where your data lives."
          },
          {
            "badge": {
              "assetRole": "award.badge",
              "alt": "Privacy seal placeholder",
              "ref": "/assets/pages/badges/badge-3.svg"
            },
            "title": "Privacy seal",
            "body": "We maintain a privacy program aligned with a placeholder privacy framework, covering data mapping, retention, subject requests and vendor review. Our data processing terms are available to every customer, and we publish a list of subprocessors that we update before any change takes effect. Every employee completes privacy training when they join and once a year after that, and new features go through a privacy review before launch, with a written assessment for anything that touches personal information. Customers can reach our privacy team directly with questions about how a specific feature handles their information, and we answer most requests within five business days, including requests to export or delete personal data. [Read our privacy terms](/terms-of-use) for the full details of how we handle personal data."
          },
          {
            "badge": {
              "assetRole": "award.badge",
              "alt": "Assured seal placeholder",
              "ref": "/assets/pages/badges/badge-4.svg"
            },
            "title": "Assured seal",
